2.47.3


From a8f660a76b033e3aaa2b58e2706d45b3ad4d47ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rations <ehqcar@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:22:07 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] vulkan/wsi: Add a RenkuOS back end (VK_RENKU_surface).

Presentation into a BView. The swapchain renders into Mesa's CPU images
(wsi_configure_cpu_image), as the headless and Win32 software back
ends do, so it works with any driver: lavapipe maps its images, a GPU
driver would blit into a host buffer. A present copies the image into
a BBitmap (B_RGB32) and makes it the view's view bitmap
(BView::SetViewBitmap). app_server keeps a reference to that bitmap
and redraws the view from it by itself, so the last frame comes back
after the window is covered, minimized or moved, with no present and
no help from the application. Two bitmaps per swapchain: the one on
screen is never written, and BView::Sync() after SetViewBitmap()
makes sure app_server has let go of the other before it is reused.

- Surface: the view's size (BView::Bounds, under the window lock) is
  the current extent. A size that cannot be read (the window busy for
  100 ms, the view moving between windows as the lock is taken) is
  reported as unknown (UINT32_MAX), never as a lost surface: the view
  outlives the surface. Formats B8G8R8A8_UNORM and _SRGB, the ones
  B_RGB32 holds without a conversion; opaque only. At least two
  images; the application gets an image back as soon as its present
  has copied it out.
- Present modes FIFO, IMMEDIATE and MAILBOX. FIFO keeps presents one
  refresh interval apart, the interval read from the main screen's
  display mode (60 Hz if the mode has no timing).
- A present after the view has changed size returns
  VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR, so the application makes a new swapchain.
- Every call on the view locks its window with a 100 ms timeout, as
  the window's thread may be waiting for the thread that presents. A
  present that cannot get the lock drops its frame and succeeds.
- Destroying a swapchain leaves its last frame on the view (app_server
  holds the bitmap), so a recreated swapchain shows no gap; destroying
  the surface clears the view bitmap.
- wsi_common.c: init, finish and surface destruction for the platform;
  meson: the back end is built with -Dplatforms=haiku, and libbe goes
  with idep_vulkan_wsi, since a static library's dependencies do not
  reach a link_whole user.

The view must outlive the surface, and the application should not draw
into it while it presents. Not done: present regions (the whole image
is copied), the present-timing extensions, colour spaces other than
sRGB, and anything faster than a copy (a shared buffer, an overlay).
FIFO is timed, not tied to the display's vertical retrace.

Tested on the build VM (nightly 95) with the Wine port's
vksurfaceprobe, a native window with a plain BView, on lavapipe with
the patched loader: 34/34 checks three times from the dev trees and
three times from the packages, reading the pixels back
from the screen (colours and orientation, FIFO 60 presents in 0.985 s
at 60 Hz, IMMEDIATE unpaced, a busy window lock dropping one frame
after 101 ms, the frame back after minimize and restore, resize with
VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR and a recreated swapchain, teardown).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/vulkan/wsi/meson.build          |   7 +-
 src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common.c         |  15 +
 src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_private.h |   7 +
 src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_renku.cpp | 710 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 738 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_renku.cpp

diff --git a/src/vulkan/wsi/meson.build b/src/vulkan/wsi/meson.build
index bc23ebe..05ae534 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/meson.build
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/meson.build
@@ -38,6 +38,11 @@ if with_platform_macos
   files_vulkan_wsi += files('wsi_common_metal.c', 'wsi_common_metal_layer.m')
 endif
 
+if with_platform_haiku
+  files_vulkan_wsi += files('wsi_common_renku.cpp')
+  platform_deps += cpp.find_library('be')
+endif
+
 if system_has_kms_drm and not with_platform_android
   files_vulkan_wsi += files('wsi_common_display.c')
 endif
@@ -88,7 +93,7 @@ else
     # our weak function overloads may not resolve properly.
     link_whole : libvulkan_wsi,
     dependencies : [
-      idep_vulkan_wsi_headers, dep_libudev
+      idep_vulkan_wsi_headers, dep_libudev, platform_deps
     ]
   )
 endif
diff --git a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common.c b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common.c
index f40f078..335af77 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common.c
@@ -269,6 +269,12 @@ wsi_device_init(struct wsi_device *wsi,
       goto fail;
 #endif
 
+#ifdef VK_USE_PLATFORM_RENKU
+   result = wsi_renku_init_wsi(wsi, alloc, pdevice);
+   if (result != VK_SUCCESS)
+      goto fail;
+#endif
+
 #ifndef VK_USE_PLATFORM_WIN32_KHR
    result = wsi_headless_init_wsi(wsi, alloc, pdevice);
    if (result != VK_SUCCESS)
@@ -358,6 +364,9 @@ wsi_device_finish(struct wsi_device *wsi,
 #if defined(VK_USE_PLATFORM_METAL_EXT)
    wsi_metal_finish_wsi(wsi, alloc);
 #endif
+#ifdef VK_USE_PLATFORM_RENKU
+   wsi_renku_finish_wsi(wsi, alloc);
+#endif
 }
 
 VKAPI_ATTR void VKAPI_CALL
@@ -383,6 +392,12 @@ wsi_DestroySurfaceKHR(VkInstance _instance,
       return;
    }
 #endif
+#ifdef VK_USE_PLATFORM_RENKU
+   if (surface->platform == VK_ICD_WSI_PLATFORM_RENKU) {
+      wsi_renku_surface_destroy(surface, _instance, pAllocator);
+      return;
+   }
+#endif
 
    vk_free2(&instance->alloc, pAllocator, surface);
 }
diff --git a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_private.h b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_private.h
index 3d2cd7d..c20f029 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_private.h
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_private.h
@@ -555,6 +555,13 @@ VkResult wsi_win32_init_wsi(struct wsi_device *wsi_device,
                          VkPhysicalDevice physical_device);
 void wsi_win32_finish_wsi(struct wsi_device *wsi_device,
                        const VkAllocationCallbacks *alloc);
+VkResult wsi_renku_init_wsi(struct wsi_device *wsi_device,
+                           const VkAllocationCallbacks *alloc,
+                           VkPhysicalDevice physical_device);
+void wsi_renku_finish_wsi(struct wsi_device *wsi_device,
+                          const VkAllocationCallbacks *alloc);
+void wsi_renku_surface_destroy(VkIcdSurfaceBase *icd_surface, VkInstance _instance,
+                               const VkAllocationCallbacks *pAllocator);
